# trivy suppression, each line with the reason it is here.
#
# CVE-2020-7665 and CVE-2020-7669 are path traversals in u-root, fixed in 0.9.0
# (2021). We build u-root from the pinned commit 869f00f6 (2026-11-17), which is
# five years newer, but Go records a local replacement as "v0.0.0" - a version
# trivy cannot order, so it reports the CVE for every such build. The code is not
# the affected one; the version string is the problem.
#
# Check before suppressing: the pinned commit in scripts/build-bb.sh must stay
# newer than 0.9.0, and u-root must not be swapped for an old tag.
CVE-2020-7665
CVE-2020-7669
